summary:
  The sleep timer's heading icon sets width itself again, inside the
  RowLayout that manages it.

history:
  Five heading icons (library, music folder, sleep timer, alarms,
  recordings) were written "width: Kirigami.Units.iconSizes.small; height:
  width" inside a RowLayout. A layout sizes its items by their implicit
  size, and Kirigami.Icon's is 32: the icons were drawn at 32 by 32 in rows
  32 to 36 high, not at the 16 the code named, the sleep timer's since its
  page was laid out on 2026-07-20 (measured in the popup offscreen at
  scales 1 and 1.75 and with a 16 pt font, 2026-11-12). Qt calls a width or
  height set on a layout's item undefined behaviour, the family the tab
  bar's 5K bug came from. The code now asks the layout for the size that
  was drawn, and the same measurement reads the same afterwards.

target:
  package/contents/ui/FullRepresentation.qml

find:
                                  source: "chronometer"
                                  Layout.preferredWidth: Kirigami.Units.iconSizes.medium

replace:
                                  source: "chronometer"
                                  width: Kirigami.Units.iconSizes.small

expect:
  Killed by the lint's qmllint pass, scripts/qmllint_gate.py: qmllint names
  the line under Quick.layout-positioning and no counted row accounts for
  it. tests/test_qmllint_gate.py::test_a_listed_exception_excuses_exactly_what_it_counts
  holds that a message without a row fails.
